  "Question": "Which 2 distances are compared in the definition of a parabola?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The sum of the distances to 2 foci",
    "B": "The distance to the focus and the distance to the directrix",
    "C": "The difference between the distances to 2 foci",
    "D": "The distance to the center of a circle"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A parabola does not have 2 foci. It is the locus of points whose distances to the focus and to the directrix are equal.",
